  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Fast-growing NATO frontline army (target 300,000) buying heavily from the US and South Korea: K2 and Abrams tanks, K9 and Krab howitzers, Homar-K and HIMARS rockets. Territorial Defence Forces (WOT) provide a local light-infantry layer. Small contingents serve with UNIFIL in Lebanon and NATO in Iraq.",
    "squad_size": 9,
    "fireteam": "Mechanised squad of 8-9 in two sections; WOT light squads of 8.",
    "tactics": [
      "combined-arms counterattack with tanks and Rosomak/Borsuk",
      "heavy artillery and rocket fires",
      "Territorial Defence ambushes and anti-drone layers in forests",
      "Spike and Javelin anti-armour teams",
      "fortified border line (East Shield) obstacles and mines as map features"
    ],
